WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.780
Passive network telemetry often gives hunters broad visibility without actively querying

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:05.670
sensitive devices.

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:10.735
It can show assets, peers, protocols, timing, and communication across trust boundaries.

00:00:10.735 --> 00:00:14.110
Protocol-aware sources may add sessions, reads, writes, commands, errors,

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:15.965
or engineering operations.

00:00:15.965 --> 00:00:20.250
Firewall, VPN, jump-host, and vendor-access logs describe boundary connections,

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:24.070
identities, source systems, approvals, destinations, and session duration.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:28.830
HMI and engineering-workstation records may add logons, processes, project access,

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:32.125
file activity, removable media, and connections to controllers.

00:00:32.125 --> 00:00:35.315
Historian data connects cyber observations to physical behavior.

00:00:35.315 --> 00:00:36.547
Trends, alarms, setpoints,

00:00:36.547 --> 00:00:40.530
and equipment state can show whether a technical event coincided with an operational

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:41.160
change.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:44.600
Authentication events add account lifecycle, failed access, privilege,

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.485
and unusual user timing.

00:00:46.485 --> 00:00:48.740
Controller change records, project repositories,

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:52.015
and management tools may report downloads, mode changes, firmware work,

00:00:52.015 --> 00:00:53.700
or configuration differences.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:57.245
These records are valuable when network traffic is encrypted or when the hunt concerns

00:00:57.245 --> 00:00:59.015
local engineering activity.

00:00:59.015 --> 00:01:00.800
Every source has blind spots.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.050
Passive sensors miss unobserved segments, serial devices behind gateways, dormant assets,

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:06.520
and local actions.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.360
Endpoint logging may be incomplete.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:11.315
Historians may show an effect without identifying who initiated it.

00:01:11.315 --> 00:01:14.130
Inconsistent clocks or asset names make correlation unreliable.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:18.490
Before hunting, document coverage, time synchronization, retention, field quality,

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:19.785
and source ownership.

00:01:19.785 --> 00:01:22.235
Protect sensitive telemetry and preserve original evidence.

00:01:22.235 --> 00:01:26.754
A strong hunt combines complementary sources, states what the data can and cannot prove,

00:01:26.754 --> 00:01:29.080
and adjusts confidence when visibility is incomplete.
